# LIUMA — environment configuration (example)
#
# Copy to `.env` for local dev, or set these in your deployment/environment
# settings. `.env` files are gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# ⚠️  Vite exposes EVERY variable prefixed with VITE_ to the PUBLIC browser
#     bundle. Only put non-sensitive, publishable values in VITE_* variables.
#     Real secrets must NOT be VITE_-prefixed and must NOT be committed.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public (safe to ship in the client bundle)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Paywall tier gating master switch. ON by default; set to "false" to disable
# (e.g. for a sandbox tenant). See src/lib/featureGates.js.
# VITE_PAYWALL_GATING_ENABLED=true

# Mercado Pago payment link for the LIUMA license (link de pago / suscripción).
# Public by nature — it is handed to every paying school. Every license notice
# (trial ending, renewal due, read-only) uses it for its "Pagar" button; while
# unset, that button opens WhatsApp to ACACIA with a prefilled message.
# See src/lib/license/billingContact.js.
# VITE_LIUMA_PAYMENT_URL=https://mpago.la/xxxxxxx

# Note: the Tier-2 support inbox (soporte@acaciaco.com.mx) is a committed
# constant in src/lib/support/constants.js (SUPPORT_EMAIL), not an env var.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only — do NOT prefix with VITE_, do NOT commit real values
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The ACACIA platform owner is identified by the base44 account role
# (role: admin), so the client needs no owner email. If a backend owner contact
# is required (e.g. for server-side notifications), set it as a base44 backend
# secret in your environment settings — keep it out of the repo and out of the
# client bundle:
# OWNER_EMAIL=owner@example.com
